<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Huldrych Zwingli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1484">1484</a>–<a href="/years/1531">1531</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Ulrich Zwingli</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Huldrych Zwingli was a Swiss priest and leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> in Zürich. After serving as parish priest at Glarus, he moved to Zürich in 1519, where his preaching led the city to abolish the Mass in 1525. His teachings shaped Reformed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestantism">Protestantism</a>. He died as a chaplain with the Zürich army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-kappel">Battle of Kappel</a> in 1531.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/huldrych-zwingli.jpg" alt="Huldrych Zwingli" width="320" height="449" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Asper · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ulrich-Zwingli-1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
